hi i'm sandy guy  product manager for alloy db for  postgres alloy tv for postgres combines  the best of google cloud with one of the  most loved open source engines postgres  to meet the needs of top-tier relational  database workloads it's a great choice  for customers looking to modernize from  their legacy proprietary databases and  for existing postgres users looking to  scale with no application changes  in this video i'm going to tell you a  little bit more about why we built alloy  db and dive into the technology that  powers it  let's get started  [Music]  we love postgres  it's open source which means you get  full portability and a license-free cost  model but it also has rich functionality  that can compete with more expensive  proprietary systems  there's a reason why it's been adopted  by millions of users in every industry  but it has some limitations especially  if you have a more demanding production  workload  some users struggle to scale and get the  performance they need from standard  postgres  maintaining high availability takes a  lot of work managing replication and  failover without tight recovery bounce  not to mention the overhead of database  maintenance and resource management  and increasingly users want to do more  with their data  generate insights and leverage aiml to  create better experiences for their end  users  alloy db addresses these challenges head  on  with industry-leading performance and  availability it can handle any workload  you throw at it while minimizing  management overhead full postgres  compatibility means regaining the  freedom to run your applications when  and where you want and benefit from the  entire postgres ecosystem let's dive  into the technology that makes this  possible  historically a postgres database runs on  a single vm with an attached disk  it's a simple setup that works both on  premise and in the cloud but doesn't  really allow you to scale  at alloy db's core is a philosophy  around disaggregation of compute and  storage at every layer of the stack  google native technologies like bigtable  and spanner have long leveraged this  approach to scale beautifully and it has  the same benefits for alloy db  it allows us to deliver not just a  scalable system but predictable high  performance both reads and rights  so what does that look like with alloy  db we began by leveraging that same  philosophy of disaggregation separating  the database layer from the storage  we created a new intelligent storage  service  optimized for postgres that scales  separately from the database layer  this architecture reduces i o  bottlenecks and offloads work like log  processing from the primary to compute  nodes within the storage layer itself  that means faster transactional  processing  alloy db is four times faster than  standard postgres for transactional  workloads  scaling happens automatically so you  won't have to provision disk and only  pay for what you use  that means if you drop a table will  automatically adjust the storage in your  cluster  notice that even within the storage  layer itself we have disaggregation of  compute and storage as well  it allows us to make performance very  predictable by automatically adding  compute resources as needed  so you don't have to worry about  hotspots and it scales really nicely  and finally the storage layer is  regional by default the primary the  failover target and read replicas all  connect to the same fundamental regional  storage layer  that makes fast bounded recovery times  and low lag read replicas possible  in the database layer we have a fully  postgres compatible database engine with  optimizations for performance and ease  of management  smart caching improves performance we  leverage both row-based and columnar  formats to meet the needs of both  transactional workloads and operational  analytics  that means alloy db is up to a hundred  times faster than standard postgres for  analytical queries  and finally we have built-in ml-enabled  adaptive systems to make management of  postgres easier than ever from memory  management to postgres vacuum  this combination of technological  advancements gives you better  availability better performance and  easier management  all with full postgres compatibility and  customer friendly pricing to learn more  about alloy dv or create an instance go  to cloud.google.com  alloy db  and stay tuned in the next few videos  we'll dive deeper into different pieces  of the architecture and show you how  they work  [Music]  you
 

